rovide resources and grants to promote online expansion of small businesses.</li>\r\n 	<li class=\"li1\"><b>European Union</b>: The EU\'s <i>Digital Europe Programme</i> provides funding for SMEs to implement digitalization across their businesses, including e-commerce. <i>COSME</i>, an EU program, also helps small businesses scale globally​.</li>\r\n 	<li class=\"li1\"><b>India</b>: Government initiatives like <i>Digital India</i> and <i>Startup India</i> provide financial support and technological assistance for e-commerce growth, especially among MSMEs.</li>\r\n 	<li class=\"li1\"><b>China</b>: The Chinese government is very supportive of e-commerce through <i>Made in China 2025</i>, encouraging digitalization and online retail. Local governments provide subsidies and grants to boost rural e-commerce.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p class=\"p2\">Most MSMEs struggle to navigate the global trading market, but with the right tools and strategies, they can overcome these challenges and achieve long-term success. By focusing on diversification, innovation, and resilience-building, MSMEs can strengthen their position and compete effectively in the dynamic global market.</p>', 'Navigating Global Trade Storms: A Roadmap for MSME Competitiveness', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '856-revision-v1', '', '', '2024-11-25 08:40:40', '2024-11-25 08:40:40', '', 856, 'https://zillioneconomy.com/?p=862', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
